Implement user story AMSD-2041: [GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Story Description
[GO, UP, MX] Live Preview of Content in CMS

## Acceptance Criteria
- 


## Root Cause Analysis & Prescribed Fix (AUTHORITATIVE — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause and prescribed the minimal fix below. This is the plan of record. Apply it; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive it.

The Acceptance Criteria above describe the desired END BEHAVIOR to VERIFY — they are NOT an implementation blueprint. Do not re-architect, split values, or add new fields/abstractions to satisfy an AC literally when the prescribed minimal fix already makes that AC pass. Implement the fix below; the ACs are how you check you got it right.

HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/services/contentstack.ts** (`options`): This is where the Contentstack SDK Stack is initialized. The options object passed to contentstack.Stack() configures api_key, delivery_token, environment, and branch — but omits the live_preview configuration entirely. Without live_preview enabled at Stack initialization, no downstream query (getEntry, getSingleEntry, ContentstackFactory) can ever fetch draft/preview content, making CMS live preview impossible across the entire application. This is the CAUSE — the computation/fetch layer — not a presentation symptom.
  - **Minimal fix:** Add a live_preview property to the options object, reading CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST from environment variables. Change the options object to include: live_preview: { preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, enable: Boolean(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN), host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST || undefined }. Also add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST to the env destructuring at lines 17-24. The Contentstack SDK's contentstack.Stack() accepts live_preview in its options — enabling it causes all queries through this Stack to include draft/preview entries when the preview token is present, which is exactly the SDK's built-in mechanism for live preview. No new query logic or factory changes are needed; the SDK handles it once the Stack is configured.


## Verification Criteria (what a tester will CONFIRM — your change must satisfy every one)
These are observable checks, derived from the acceptance criteria and description. They describe WHAT is observed, not how to build it. Make the minimal change that makes all of these true; your accompanying test should assert them:
- When a content author edits content in the CMS without publishing it, opening the application's preview shows that unpublished edit rendered on the page.
- The unpublished-edit preview renders correctly for the GO Transit brand experience.
- The unpublished-edit preview renders correctly for the UP Express brand experience.
- The unpublished-edit preview renders correctly for the MX brand experience.
- When an author makes a further unpublished edit and reloads the preview, the newest version of the content is displayed without any publish step being performed.
- Previewed unpublished content of different kinds — body text, images, hyperlinks, tabular content, and collections of cards — is rendered as fully formatted page output, not as raw or broken content.
- Content that has only been edited but never published does not appear on the publicly accessible site seen by regular visitors.

